IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oa3-helpers`
IMPORT `oa3-part1-applications`

-- Tests of oa3-part1-applications.l4 (regs 3 to 5 and 10 to 12). Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of the
-- regulation; each date edge is tested on both sides, and each rule that can answer "not covered" is asked a case that does.

-- Reg 3(1): the form is required only where the Minister requires it.
#ASSERT `reg 3(1): the application has the form the Minister requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 3(1): the application has the form the Minister requires` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 3(1): the application has the form the Minister requires` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 3(1): the application has the form the Minister requires` FALSE TRUE
-- Reg 3(2): an application is deemed made when a completed form is received, unless the Act (ss 5(2), 11(3)) deems it made.
#ASSERT `reg 3(2): the application is deemed to have been made` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 3(2): the application is deemed to have been made` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 3(2): the application is deemed to have been made` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 3(2): the application is deemed to have been made` TRUE TRUE
-- Reg 4(1): someone may act for a person the Minister considers unable for a sufficient reason.
#ASSERT `reg 4(1): a responsible person or agency may make the request, appeal, application, statement or notice on the person's behalf` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 4(1): a responsible person or agency may make the request, appeal, application, statement or notice on the person's behalf` FALSE)
-- Reg 4(2): the provincial authority may apply for a PENSION for a person who is or has been on UAA or CAP assistance.
#ASSERT `reg 4(2): the appropriate provincial authority may make the application on the person's behalf` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `reg 4(2): the appropriate provincial authority may make the application on the person's behalf` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 4(2): the appropriate provincial authority may make the application on the person's behalf` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 4(2): the appropriate provincial authority may make the application on the person's behalf` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 4(2): the appropriate provincial authority may make the application on the person's behalf` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 4(2): the appropriate provincial authority may make the application on the person's behalf` FALSE TRUE FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 5(1)(a) and (b): the Minister is satisfied, and approves after the last day of the month of receipt.
-- Received 2020-03-15: the last day of the month is 2020-03-31, so approval on 2020-04-01 is after it and on 2020-03-31 is not.
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
-- Received 2020-02-10: 2020 is a leap year, so the month ends 2020-02-29.
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 2 10)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 5(1): the approval of the application for a pension is within subsection (1)` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2020 2 10))

-- Reg 5(1): the latest of the day received, the day qualified and the date the applicant specified.
-- Received 2020-03-15, qualified 2019-12-01, nothing specified: the day received.
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 12 1) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 3 15
-- Qualified later than received: the day qualified.
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 1) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 5 1
-- A date specified later than both: that date. Earlier than the day received: ignored. Equal: the same day.
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 12 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 7 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 7 1
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 12 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 12 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 5(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 5 1

-- Reg 5(2): the applicant attained 65 BEFORE the day the application was received.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the applicant attained the age of 65 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the applicant attained the age of 65 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 14) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 5(2): the applicant attained the age of 65 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 5(2): the applicant attained the age of 65 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
-- Reg 5(2): the latest of one year before the day received (here 2019-03-15), the day 65 was attained, the day qualified,
-- and the first day of the month before the date specified.
-- Nothing recent: the day one year before the day received.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2018 6 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 6 1) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 15
-- Turned 65 within the year: the day 65 was attained.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 8 20
-- Qualified later than 65: the day qualified.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 11 1) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 11 1
-- Date specified 2020-02-10: the month immediately before is January 2020, so 2020-01-01.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 2 10)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 1 1
-- Date specified 2019-09-30: August 2019, so 2019-08-01, which is before the day 65 was attained (2019-08-20): the latter stands.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 9 30)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 8 20
-- The same specified date with 65 attained 2019-07-01: 2019-08-01 is the latest.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 7 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 9 30)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 8 1
-- Date specified in January: the month before is the previous December.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 7 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 7 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 1 15)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 12 1
-- Received on a leap day: one year before clamps to 2019-02-28.
#ASSERT `reg 5(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 2 28

-- Reg 5 as a whole (arguments: satisfied, approved, received, 65 attained, qualified, specified).
-- The Minister is not satisfied: the Regulations give no day.
#ASSERT `reg 5: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for a pension is effective` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Approved within the month of receipt: subsection (1)(b) fails, no day (not covered).
#ASSERT `reg 5: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for a pension is effective` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Turned 65 before the application was received: subsection (2) governs.
#ASSERT `reg 5: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for a pension is effective` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20)
-- Turned 65 on the day the application was received: not before, so subsection (1) governs.
#ASSERT `reg 5: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for a pension is effective` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 1) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
-- Applied before turning 65 (2020-03-20): subsection (1), the latest of 03-15, 03-20 and the day received.
#ASSERT `reg 5: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for a pension is effective` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) NOTHING EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20)

-- Reg 5(3) and (4): a deemed or waived application takes effect on the day the person attained 65.
#ASSERT `reg 5(3): the day on which the Minister's approval of the deemed application is effective` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1)
#ASSERT `reg 5(3): the day on which the Minister's approval of the deemed application is effective` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 5(4): the day on which the Minister's approval is effective where the requirement for an application is waived` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1)
#ASSERT `reg 5(4): the day on which the Minister's approval is effective where the requirement for an application is waived` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1) EQUALS NOTHING

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 10, 10.1 and 11.
#ASSERT `reg 10: the Minister must approve the application for a supplement by the pensioner in accordance with section 11 of the Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 10: the Minister must approve the application for a supplement by the pensioner in accordance with section 11 of the Act` FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 10.1: the day on which the Minister's approval of the supplement is effective where the requirement for an application is waived` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1)
#ASSERT `reg 10.1: the day on which the Minister's approval of the supplement is effective where the requirement for an application is waived` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2018 5 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 11: the Minister must approve the application for an allowance` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 11: the Minister must approve the application for an allowance` FALSE)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Reg 12(1): approval after the last day of the month of receipt (received 2020-03-15: the month ends 2020-03-31).
#ASSERT `reg 12(1): the approval of the application for an allowance is after the last day of the month in which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(1): the approval of the application for an allowance is after the last day of the month in which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
-- Reg 12(1): the later of the day received and the day entitled.
#ASSERT `reg 12(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 12(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 5 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 5 1
#ASSERT `reg 12(1): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2020 3 15
-- Reg 12(2): the spouse attained 60 before the day received.
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner attained the age of 60 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 10) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner attained the age of 60 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 14) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner attained the age of 60 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner attained the age of 60 years before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 16) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
-- Reg 12(2): the latest of one year before the day received (2019-03-15), the day 60 was attained and the day entitled under s 19.
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2018 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 8 20
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 12 31) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 12 31
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 3 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 12(2): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 3 14) (YearMonthDay 2019 3 14) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 15
-- Reg 12(3): the survivor became entitled before the day received.
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(3): the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 12(3): the survivor became entitled to an allowance under section 21 of the Act before the day on which the application was received` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 16) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15))
-- Reg 12(3): the later of one year before the day received (2019-03-15) and the day entitled under s 21.
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2018 1 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 6 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 6 1
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 3 15) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 3 14) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 15
-- Received on a leap day: one year before is 2019-02-28.
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2019 2 27) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 2 28
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2019 2 28) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 2 28
#ASSERT `reg 12(3): the day on which the approval is effective` (YearMonthDay 2020 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2019 3 1) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2019 3 1

-- Reg 12 as a whole (arguments: applicant, approved, received, 60 attained, entitled).
-- A spouse who turned 60 before the day received: subsection (2), whenever the approval comes (even in the month of receipt).
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20)
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 8 20)
-- A spouse who turns 60 on the day received: subsection (1), and only when approved after the month ends.
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(2): the spouse or common-law partner of a pensioner` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A survivor entitled before the day received: subsection (3).
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(3): a survivor` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2019 6 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 6 1)
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(3): a survivor` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2018 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 3 15)
-- A survivor entitled on or after the day received: subsection (1).
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(3): a survivor` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15)
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(3): a survivor` (YearMonthDay 2020 4 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20)
#ASSERT `reg 12: the day on which the Minister's approval of the application for an allowance is effective` `reg 12(3): a survivor` (YearMonthDay 2020 3 31) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 15) (YearMonthDay 2000 1 1) (YearMonthDay 2020 3 20) EQUALS NOTHING
